From 68fceb32271112d97c4b53c6520edcc7ed58df44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cline-fork-rebase <cline-fork-rebase@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:22:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] fix(core): do not count a wait that is sent again as a
 loop

- Keep the loop guard for identical tool calls that return quickly.
  Three identical calls in a row still warn and five still stop the run.
- Do not count a repeat of an identical call when the earlier identical
  call blocked for at least the threshold. Give such a repeat no warning
  either. The threshold is half of HAMH_WAIT_S, at most 50 seconds and
  at least 5 seconds.
  HAMH_WAIT_S is the bound of one wait on a background job, in seconds,
  as the harness sets it. Without it nothing is exempt.
- Stop the threshold at 50 seconds because the waits that sessions send
  are shorter than half of a long bound. Rules files name a wait of 100
  seconds, and the harness's default bound is 240 seconds.
- Cap the time the exempt repeats of one run of identical calls may take.
  HAMH_WAIT_CAP_S sets the cap in seconds. The default is two hours.
  Past the cap the repeats count again, from where the count stood.
- Judge by how long a call blocked, never by its text.
  SessionRuntime tells the tracker how long each finished call took.
- A session that waits for a long background job sends one bounded wait
  again and again while the job runs. In a live run the guard ended a
  prompt at the fifth identical wait although the job was still running.
- Before the change, 14 of the new tests failed. All 88 tests of the two
  files pass after it. loop-detection.test.ts is new and has 13 tests.
